{
  "summary": "Prevents wallet fee-bumped transactions from receiving an nLockTime older than the transaction they replace. When creating a replacement via bumpfee, the original transaction's locktime is recorded in CCoinControl and passed to DiscourageFeeSniping as a floor for any random backdating.",
  "problem": "Bitcoin Core's anti-fee-sniping randomly backdates transaction locktimes by up to 99 blocks approximately 10% of the time. When bumping fees, this random backdating can cause a replacement transaction to have an earlier locktime than the original, creating an unnatural on-chain pattern that acts as a fingerprint identifying Bitcoin Core or Electrum wallets.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'We also conducted a small analysis to see how many the backdating in RBF transactions actually happen. We have data on the replaced transactions from 2025-05-01 to 2026-06-01... on average there are only about 200-300 hundred replaccements backdating per week. Looking at the percentages we see that on average is less than 2% of all the transactions that have been replaced.'",
    "Linked issue #26526."
  ],
